.TH "GMB" "1" "Sep 2026" "GlassMarble 1.1.0" "GlassMarble Manual"

.SH NAME
gmb-doc-eval - Score managed sections for faithfulness against fresh FactSheets


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb doc eval [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Scores every non-empty managed section against a freshly assembled
FactSheet using the deterministic faithfulness scorer (no network, no AKG
required). Score = supported claims / total claims (RAGAS formula).

.PP
Exit codes:
  0  Global score at or above --min-score
  1  Global score below --min-score


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for eval

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Emit machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--min-score\fP=0.75
	Minimum global faithfulness (exit 1 below)

.PP
\fB--sample\fP=0
	Maximum sections to score (0 = all)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gmb doc eval
  gmb doc eval --sample 20 --min-score 0.9 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmb-doc(1)\fP


